/*!
\page page_stTpcHit StTpcHit

\brief Reconstructed hit (cluster) in the STAR Time Projection Chamber.

\ref StTpcHit represents a single reconstructed cluster in the STAR TPC or its inner upgrade
(iTPC). It is produced by the TPC cluster-finder (FCF or TCL) during the reconstruction chain
and stored in \ref StTpcHitCollection. In addition to the position, charge, and hardware address
inherited from \ref StHit, \ref StTpcHit stores the cluster extent in pad and time-bucket
coordinates, the raw ADC sum, and optional recalibration data used by the dE/dx analysis.

\section sec_tpchit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StMeasuredPoint
        └── StHit
            └── StTpcHit         (concrete — this class)
\endverbatim

Objects are stored in \c StSPtrVecTpcHit inside \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection →
\ref StTpcSectorHitCollection → \ref StTpcHitCollection → StEvent framework.

\section sec_tpchit_hwpack Hardware Address Packing (mHardwarePosition)

The 32-bit \c mHardwarePosition field is packed as follows:

| Bits | Width | Meaning | Accessor |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1 | iTPC flag (1 = iTPC sector) | detector() |
| 4–8 | 5 | Sector number (1–24) | sector() |
| 9–15 | 7 | Padrow number (1–128) | padrow() |
| 22–31 | 10 | Pixel count (TCL) / time-bucket count (FCF) | pixelsInHit() |

\section sec_tpchit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_tpchit_inherited Inherited (selected)
- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Packed sector/padrow/iTPC flag (see table above).
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPosition</tt> — 3-D hit centroid in STAR global frame (cm).
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-sigma position uncertainties in cm.
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Calibrated cluster charge from the gain tables.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — FCF cluster status flags (see <tt>FCF_flags</tt> in
  <tt>StRoot/StDaqLib/TPC/trans_table.hh</tt>).

\subsection subsec_tpchit_own StTpcHit-specific
- <tt>UChar_t mMinpad</tt> — Offset from centroid pad to the lowest pad in the cluster.
  Absolute pad: <tt>round(mMcl_x/64) − mMinpad</tt>.
- <tt>UChar_t mMaxpad</tt> — Offset from centroid pad to the highest pad.
  Absolute pad: <tt>round(mMcl_x/64) + mMaxpad</tt>.
- <tt>UChar_t mMintmbk</tt> — Offset from centroid time bucket to the first time bucket.
- <tt>UChar_t mMaxtmbk</tt> — Offset from centroid time bucket to the last time bucket.
- <tt>Short_t mMcl_x</tt> — Cluster centroid pad position × 64 (fixed-point, 1/64 pad
  resolution). Use <tt>pad()</tt> for the floating-point value.
- <tt>Short_t mMcl_t</tt> — Cluster centroid time bucket × 64 (fixed-point, 1/64 bin
  resolution). Use <tt>timeBucket()</tt> for the floating-point value.
- <tt>UShort_t mAdc</tt> — Raw ADC sum of all pixels in the cluster.
- <tt>Float_t mChargeModified</tt> — <b>Transient</b> (<tt>//!</tt>). Recalibrated charge from
  \c StdEdxY2Maker; zero if not set.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionU</tt> — <b>Transient</b>. Upper pad-row edge position
  (y_local + padlength/2) in global frame (cm).
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionL</tt> — <b>Transient</b>. Lower pad-row edge position
  (y_local − padlength/2) in global frame (cm).
- <tt>Float_t mdX</tt> — <b>Transient</b>. Track path length through pad row for dE/dx (cm).

\section sec_tpchit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns \c kiTpcId or \c kTpcId based on bit 1 of
  the hardware position.
- <tt>UInt_t sector() const</tt> — Sector number 1–24 (bits 4–8).
- <tt>UInt_t padrow() const</tt> — Padrow number 1–128 (bits 9–15).
- <tt>UInt_t padsInHit() const</tt> — Number of pads fired.
- <tt>UChar_t minPad() / maxPad() const</tt> — Lowest/highest pad in cluster.
- <tt>Short_t minTmbk() / maxTmbk() const</tt> — First/last time bucket in cluster.
- <tt>Short_t timeBucketsInHit() const</tt> — Number of time buckets fired.
- <tt>Float_t pad() const</tt> — Centroid pad (floating-point): <tt>mMcl_x / 64.0</tt>.
- <tt>Float_t timeBucket() const</tt> — Centroid time bucket (floating-point):
  <tt>mMcl_t / 64.0</tt>.
- <tt>UShort_t adc() const</tt> — Raw ADC sum.
- <tt>Float_t chargeModified() const</tt> — Transient recalibrated charge.
- <tt>Float_t dX()</tt> — Transient dE/dx path length (cm).
- <tt>Int_t volumeID() const</tt> — Combined ID: <tt>100 × sector() + padrow()</tt>.
- <tt>void setExtends(cl_x, cl_t, mnpad, mxpad, mntmbk, mxtmbk)</tt> — Sets centroid and
  extent fields from absolute min/max values.
- <tt>Bool_t IsSortable() / Int_t Compare(const TObject*) const</tt> — Supports sorting by
  sector, padrow, then |z|.

\section sec_tpchit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StTpcHit uses a custom memory pool (\c StMemoryPool) via overloaded \c new/delete.
Objects are owned by \ref StTpcPadrowHitCollection which explicitly deletes them in its
destructor. <b>Do not delete StTpcHit* pointers obtained from the collection.</b>

\section sec_tpchit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StTpcHitCollection* tpcColl = event->tpcHitCollection();
if (!tpcColl) return;

// Iterate sector 1 (0-based index 0), padrow 13 (0-based index 12)
const StTpcSectorHitCollection* sec = tpcColl->sector(0);
if (!sec) return;
const StTpcPadrowHitCollection* row = sec->padrow(12);
if (!row) return;

for (const StTpcHit* hit : row->hits()) {
    if (!hit->usedInFit()) continue;
    std::cout << "sec=" << hit->sector()
              << " row=" << hit->padrow()
              << " pad=" << hit->pad()
              << " t=" << hit->timeBucket()
              << " q=" << hit->charge()
              << " adc=" << hit->adc() << "\n";
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_sthit, \ref page_stmeasuredpoint, \ref page_stTpcHitCollection
*/
